> So fix the interpreter.  That sort of behavior is completely broken.
> Spaces are valid in filenames, whether you like it or not.

Well, the problem is that in (almost?) every command line interpreter, not
just all unix shells and windows, a space is used to separate the command
from the variables and options, and to separate the individual variables
and options.

Therefore, allowing spaces in filenames will *always* be a problem if you
allow using them as (part of) a variable or option, unless you introduce
make-do fixes like single/double quotes. Of course, introducing quotes
introduces the problem of not easily being able to use those in filenames,
usually circumvented by doubling them ('', not ").

